abstract: "Audio-language models often follow text that conflicts with audio, even when the audio evidence is clear. We examine whether the audio-supported answer is unavailable or represented but overridden in arbitration, and propose Gated Audio Counterfactual Logit Correction (GACL), a training-free decoding rule for repairing reversals."
keywords:
  - audio-language models
  - multimodal arbitration
  - training-free decoding
  - contrastive decoding
